    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15942" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕpĭdĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Roman rhetorician</i>, <i>teacher of
				M. Antony and Augustus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 17,
				25, 38, § 243</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Rhet.
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Marullus, <i>a tribune of the people in the time of
				Caesar</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 79 sq.</span></i>†
			‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpĭdixis</span></b> , is,
				f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδειζις</span>,
				<i>a specimen of acting</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 2620</span></i>.</div>
